nts for winner and loser; check if winner reaches 3 (then print winner and number of fights so far + 1).\n- Update the queue: in case challenger wins, push old king to back and king becomes challenger; in case king wins, push challenger to back and king stays.\n- Update hq and hc incrementally; maintain powB_k1 = BASE^(k-1) for updating hq. Use a large BASE and 64-bit overflow to create a rolling hash; use XOR-based updates for consec with pre-generated random values.\n- After each fight, compute the new state (hq, hc, king) and check if it has appeared; if yes, output -1 -1; else insert and continue.\n- Output exactly: ruler_index fights_count when a ruler is found, or -1 -1 if a cycle is detected.\n\nThis approach provides a complete solution within the constraints and handles edge cases like the first fight, cycle detection, and the ruler condition. It uses deterministic randomized hashing (with a fixed seed) for reproducibility across runs in this environment.",
