- X_max = floor(min_k (S_k_max - P_k)/k)
- TOT = product_i (c_i + 1) mod 1e9+7

Then for each integer x in (X_min, X_max], we can run a dynamic programming over k to count sequences with the prefix sum constraints. Specifically, define dp[s] as the number of ways to obtain partial sum s after processing first k elements, with s constrained to be >= B_k(x). Transition uses a sliding window (prefix sums) to account for a_k in [0, c_k]:

